  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "0.36 g water drop has $\\frac{0.36}{18}$ moles\n$\\frac{0.36}{18}$ moles of water has $\\frac{0.36}{18} \\times 6.023 \\times 10^{23}$ molecules of water \n 1 molecule of water has 1 oxygen atom.\n$\\therefore$ Number of O atoms $=\\frac{0.36}{18} \\times 6.023 \\times 10^{23}=1.205 \\times 10^{22}$",
    "image": null
  },
